{"GoogleCalendarService calls SelectedCalendarRepository.updateManyByCredentialId with an empty data object, which forwards directly to Prisma updateMany, preventing the intended timestamp touch and potentially causing Prisma validation failures in the webhook/sync path": 0.9385778307914734, "connectedCalendarsHandler exposes Prisma Date values as cacheUpdatedAt through tRPC while CredentialActionsDropdown types and consumes the prop as a client Date, creating an unsafe serialization contract across the server/client boundary that can cause inconsistent date handling or hydration/runtime issues": 0.4273887872695923, "SelectedCalendar.updatedAt refresh lacks failure-path coverage - a repository failure after cache writes succeed would turn an otherwise successful refresh into an exception": 0.8376508355140686, "SelectedCalendar.updatedAt refresh has no coverage for when a credential has zero selected calendars, making the write a no-op and potentially hiding stale timestamps in the UI": 0.8420055508613586}